# Certificates that the TLS connections of the Pomdog examples distrust.
#
# distrusted-keys-gen converts this file into the SHA-256 hashes of their
# public keys (SubjectPublicKeyInfo). A TLS connection fails when a certificate
# anywhere in the server's chain has one of these keys, so an entry also covers
# every other certificate of its key, such as a cross-signed copy.
#
# NOTE: The eMudhra intermediate CAs below had private keys that anyone could
# recover from their public certificates (October 2026). Sectigo also
# cross-signed each one under AAA Certificate Services, with the same key.
# See https://kudelskisecurity.com/research/emudhra-intermediate-ca-private-key-compromise

